hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4126","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace When he came to Mecca, he entered it from its top and left from its bottom.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4127","Hanad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Hatem bin Ismail, on the authority of Aflah bin Humaid, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “We went out With the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performing Hajj at leisure during the months and days of Hajj, until we presented an extravagance. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And he greeted his companions: Whoever among you has not brought a sacrifice and would like to perform Hajj with Umrah, let him do so. She said: The one who takes that is among the companions of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the one who left. As for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the powerful of his companions, they had a sacrificial animal with them. They will perform Hajj. She said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me while I was crying and I had begun performing Hajj. He said: What makes you cry? I said: I am deprived I am not performing Umrah. He said: You are only a woman from the daughters of Adam. God has decreed for you what He has decreed for them, so continue your Hajj, and God may He will provide for you. She said: So we went out until God had completed our Hajj and I had finished. Then we departed from Mina and camped on the night of the measles. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Bakr, and he said: Take your sister out of the Haram, and let her perform Umrah. Then they finished. I I am waiting for you here, so we came to him at night, and he said: Have you finished? I said: Yes, so he gave permission to leave, so we passed by the house and the Messenger of God went around him. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, then he left before dawn.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4128","Ubayd Allah bin Sa`id reported, saying: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi`, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He said the salutation when he left the armies and companies, or Hajj or Umrah, if he fulfilled his duty in a second or second place. He said the takbir three times, then said: “There is no god.” Except God alone, He has no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things. We are repentant, worshipers, prostrate to our Lord, thankful. It is true. God kept His promise, helped His servant, and defeated the parties alone.”"
"4129","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. When he departed from Hajj, Umrah, or a campaign, and paid a large portion of the earth, he said: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner. To Him belongs the dominion, and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things. They are worshipers of our Lord, prostrating themselves. God has fulfilled His promise, and He has helped His servant, and he has been defeated. \"The parties alone\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4130","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh reported, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: Malik told me that Nafi’ told them, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, “that When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned from Hajj and Umrah, he would go to Al-Batha’ in Dhul-Hulayfah and pray there. Nafi’ said: Abdullah bin Omar used to do that."
"4131","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id reported, saying: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Muwarriq, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Ja`far, he said: “The Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, when he came from a journey he would meet the children of his household, and he once came from a journey and he carried me in his hands, and someone came My son Fatima, and he followed him behind him, so we entered the city as three on an animal.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4132","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Ishaq told us, he said: Anas bin Malik told us, he said: “I was with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, closed his door from Usfan until we were on some road, and Safiyya bint Huyyi was sent to her by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, behind him, and his she-camel stumbled and killed him. Abu Talha rushed in and said: May God make me your ransom, O Messenger of God. He said: The woman is upon you. So he turned his garment over his face until he came to her, then he threw it on her and fixed their boat for them, so they embarked and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, surrounded us. He greeted us, and when he overlooked the city, he said: “We are repentant, we are worshipers of our Lord, and we are thankful.” He continued to say that until we entered the city."
"4133","Ali bin Hajar reported, saying: Ismail told us, saying: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, “Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came from a journey... Then he looked at the walls of the city and positioned his mount, and if he were on an animal he pulled it from its side.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4134","Abu Al-Ash’ath and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ reported, saying: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, he said: Habib bin Al-Shahid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abu Mulaika, and Muhammad said: Ibn Abi Mulaika told us, Ibn al-Zubayr said to Ibn Ja’far: “Remember when Muhammad said: On the day we met the Messenger of God May God bless him and grant him peace, you and I, and Ibn Abbas said: Yes, he carried us and left you? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4135","Suleiman bin Salam reported, he said: Al-Nadr reported, he said: Suleiman told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, presented So the Sudan of Medina received him, marshalling and saying, “Muhammad, a righteous man, has come according to their words.” Anas did not mention that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4136","Ali bin Al-Hussein reported, he said: Umayyah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, he said: “When the Ansar Hajj did not enter through its doors, but entered from the backs of its houses, so God revealed, “And there is no righteousness that you enter houses from their backs.”"
"4137","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Adi bin Hamra Al-Zuhri. He said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, standing on his mount, saying: By God, you are the best of God’s earth and the most beloved of God’s earth.” To God, and had I not come out of you, I would not have left.”"
"4138","Ishaq bin Mansour reported, he said: Yaqoub informed me, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu told me Salamah bin Abdul Rahman said that Abdullah bin Adi bin Al Hamra told him that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was standing On his mount in Mecca, he said to Mecca: “By God, you are the best of God’s earth and the most beloved of God’s land. Had I not been expelled from you, I would not have left.”"
"4139","Salama bin Shabib reported, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Khaled, who said: I heard Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in the Al-Jazura market in Mecca: “By God, you are the best land of God and the most beloved country to God. Had I not I got out of you what I got out.”"
"4140","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Yunus bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Ali bin Hussein He told him: Amr bin Othman told him, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, that he said: O Messenger of God, will you stay in your house in Mecca?"
"4141","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ narrated, saying: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, saying: Muammar narrated, on the authority of al-Zuhri, and Ishaq ibn Mansour narrated, saying: Abd al-Razzaq narrated, He said: Muammar and Al-Awza’i reported on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ali bin Husayn, on the authority of Amr bin Uthman, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd. He said: “I said: Oh Messenger of God, where shall we camp tomorrow? That was during his Hajj. He said: Did Aqeel leave a house for us? : The hadith of Al-Awza’i is not preserved (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4142","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “The Antichrist will not enter Mecca or Medina.”"
"4143","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna reported, on the authority of al-Hajjaj, he said: Hammad told us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind reported, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Fatima bint Qais, “that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came one day quickly and ascended the pulpit, and it was announced among the people that prayer is unified, so the people gathered. He said: Oh O people, I did not invite you because of a desire or fear that has descended upon you, but Tamim al-Dari informed me that a group of the people of Palestine They rode the sea, and the wind blew them to one of the islands of the sea, and lo, they were like a hairy animal, and it was not known whether it was male or female His large hair. They said: Who are you? She said: I am al-Jasassah. They said: So tell us. She said: I am not your informant, nor am I. I asked you to inform you, but in this monastery there is a poor man until he informs you and until he informs you. So they came to the monastery, and they found a man. A blind man bound in iron. He said: Who are you? They said: We are the Arabs. He said: Was the Prophet sent? They said: Yes. He said: Did the Arabs follow him? They said: Yes, he said: That is better for them, then he said: What did Fares do? Has he appeared on her? They said: He has not appeared on her yet, so he said: As for it? He will appear on it, then he said: What did the spring of Zaghr do? They said: It was filled with water. What did Lake Tiberias do? They said: It was filled with water. He said: So what did it do? What about the palm trees of Baysan? They said: It had fed its first, so it jumped so much that we feared it would escape, so we said: Who are you? He said: I am the Antichrist As for me, I will trample the entire earth except Mecca and Taybah. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: So rejoice, O community of Muslims, this is Taybah. \"He enters it\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4144","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Shabi, he said: Fatima bint Qays said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “Indeed, there was no prophet before me who did not warn his nation of the Antichrist, and he is among you, O nation, and he will tread on an entire earth that is not good. “This is good.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4145","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Sammak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “Indeed, God named the city Taybah.”"
"4146","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, who said: I heard Abu Al-Hubab Saeed bin Yasar say: I heard Abu Hurairah He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was ordered to go to a town that eats up towns. They say: Yathrib, and it is the city that purifies the people just as it purifies \"The furnace is the dross of iron.\""
"4147","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Abdul Rahman told us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: “ A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and pledged his allegiance to Islam. Then he came the next day feverish and said: Give me a ride three times, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “The city is like a kir; it expels its impurity and exudes its goodness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4148","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Ma’an told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of Sufyan bin Abi Zuhayr, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Yemen will be conquered and a people will come dressed in Then they will be patient with their families and those who obey them, and Medina will be better for them, if they only knew. And the Levant will be conquered and a people will come to flee. Then they will be patient with their families and those who obey them, and Medina would be better for them, if they had known. And Iraq will be conquered and a people will arrive refuge. Then they will be patient with their families and those who obey them, and Medina is better for them, if they only knew.”"
"4149","Muhammad ibn Adam told me, on the authority of Abdah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Sufyan ibn Abi Zuhair, The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Yemen will be conquered, and a people will come there, dressing, and they will take care of their families and those who obey them, and Medina is better.” For them, if they only knew. Then Iraq will be conquered, and a people will come running wild, and they will take charge of their families and those who obeyed them, and Medina. It would be better for them, if they had known. Then the Levant will be conquered, and a people will come to flee, and they will take care of their families and those who obey them, and Medina. “It would be better for them, if they had known.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4150","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi reported, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Muslim bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Khallad, He was one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever fears the people of Medina, God will fear him.” And upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all of mankind. No deed or justice will be accepted from him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4151","Ali ibn Hajr ibn Iyas reported on the authority of Ismail, who is ibn Jafar, on the authority of Yazid, who is ibn Khusayfa, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd. Allah bin Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Sa’sa’ah, that Ata’ bin Yasar told him that Al-Sa’ib bin Khallad, the brother of Al-Harith bin Al-Khazraj, He told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever fears the people of Medina by being unjust to them, God will fear him, and a curse will be upon him.” God, the angels, and all of mankind, neither slander nor justice will be accepted from Him.”"
"4152","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Omar bin Nabih told us, he said: Abu Abdullah Al-Qarraaz told me, he said: I heard Saad bin Malik said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever intends harm against the people of Medina, God will dissolve him just as salt dissolves in \"water\""
"4153","Ubayd Allah bin Sa`id reported to Abu Qudama al-Sarkhasi, saying: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abu Mawdud told me, he said: I heard Abu Abdullah Al-Qarraaz says: Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever intends harm to the people of Medina, God will melt him just as he is melted.” \"salt in the water\""
"4154","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “O God, bless them in their measure, and bless them in their struggle and in their debt,” meaning the people of Medina."
"4155","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of Amr bin Sulaym Al-Zarqi, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali bin Abi A student, he said: “We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until he was at Al-Harra with the watering can that had belonged to Saad bin Abi Waqqas. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Bring me an ablution. He performed ablution, then he got up and faced the Qiblah, then he said: O God, Abraham was Your servant and your friend prayed for blessing for the people of Mecca, and I, Muhammad, your servant and messenger, pray for the people of Medina to bless them in their era. “And their share is equal to what you have blessed for the people of Mecca, with two blessings.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4156","Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad reported, saying: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Salih bin Kaysan told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, On the authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, make Medina beloved to us as You have made it beloved to us.” Mecca or more severe, O God, bless for us its fast and its tide, and transfer its epidemic to Mahay’ah.”"
"4157","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Urwa On the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at the sky and said: “O God, make Medina beloved to us as You have made Mecca dearer to us, or more, O God, bless for us its fast and its tide, and transfer its affliction to its abode, which is Al-Juhfa.”"
"4158","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nu’aym al-Mujmar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The city does not Neither the plague nor the antichrist will enter it.”"
"4159","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Omar bin Abdul-Wahid reported, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no country but the Antichrist will trample it except Medina and Mecca, on every corner of the earth.” The angels are pure and guarding the city, and the marsh descends and the city shakes with three tremors, and every hypocrite and infidel comes out of it.”"
"4160","Abu Dawud reported, he said: Ya’qub told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah told me, Abu Sa`id Al-Khudri said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us a long story about the Antichrist. He said: It was in what he told us, he said: “He will come It is forbidden for him to enter the city, so he will end up in some marshes next to the city, and he will emerge there on that day, meaning a better man. people, or from the best of people, and he says to him: I bear witness that you are the Antichrist whose hadith was narrated to us by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Antichrist says: Do you think that if I killed this man and brought him back to life, would you have any doubts about the matter? They said: No. He said: Then he kills him and then brings him back to life. Then he says: When he brings him back to life: By God, I have never been more discerning about you than I am now. The Antichrist wants to kill him, but he will not gain power over him.”"
"4161","Hammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim reported, saying: My father told us, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, that he told him on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Mawla Al-Mahri, that Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said: “We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Oh God, Abraham made Mecca sacred.” So he made it forbidden, and I have made the city forbidden for the period between its two crises - that no blood be shed in it, that no weapons be carried in it for battle, and that no confusion be made in it. A tree except for fodder, O God, bless our city, O God, bless our hardship, O God, bless our cities, O God, bless us in Our hardship, O God, bless our cities for us, O God, bless our city for us, O God, make with the blessing two blessings, and by the One in whose hand is my soul. From the city of Shuaib and there is no censure except over it two angels guarding it.”"
"4162","Bishr ibn Khalid reported, he said: Ghandar reported, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of al-Harith ibn Suwayd, he said: It was said: Ali: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, singled you out for something rather than people in general. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not single us out for anything that was not It concerns the people. There is nothing in the sheath of this sword of mine. So he took a scroll containing some of the teeth of a camel, and on it was: “The city is a sanctuary from a bull to a caravan.” Whoever commits an offense therein or harbors an infidel, the curse of God, the angels, and all of mankind will be upon him, and it will not be accepted from him on the Day of Resurrection. Punishment and no justice. The obligation of Muslims is the same. Whoever betrays a Muslim will be subject to the curse of God, the angels, and all of mankind. Punishment will not be accepted from him. And there is no justice.”"
"4163","Ismail bin Masoud reported, saying: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, He said: We have nothing except the Book of God and this document from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Medina is a sanctuary from a cart to a bull from Whoever commits a crime therein or harbors an infidel, upon him will be the curse of God, the angels, and all of mankind. No sin or justice will be accepted from him. He is a guarantor of the Muslims. One time. So whoever betrays a Muslim, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all of mankind. No negligence or justice will be accepted from him. And whoever leads a people unjustly. Then, his master, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all of mankind. No good deeds or justice will be accepted from him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4164","Ayoub bin Muhammad Al-Wazzan told me, he said: Marwan told us, he said: Othman bin Hakim told us, he said: Amer bin Saad told me, about His father, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No one leaves the city seeking it unless God gives it something better than him, nor Anyone who endures its effort and hardship will remain steadfast therein until he dies therein, unless I will be a witness or intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection, and what is in between will be forbidden. It refuses to have its limbs cut off or its game killed, and no one of the people of Medina intends harm unless God melts him in the fire as lead melts or Dissolving the salt in the water.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4165","Qutaibah bin Sa’id reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, the client of Al-Mahri, that Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “No one is patient with the struggle of Medina and its people and dies unless I am his intercessor or A martyr on the Day of Resurrection if he is a Muslim.”"
"4166","Qutaybah bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Qatn bin Wahb bin Uwaymir bin Al-Ajja’, that the servant of Al-Zubayr was being impure. He told him that he He was sitting with Abdullah bin Omar in the house, when a female servant of his came to him to ask, and she said: I want to go out, Abu Abdul Rahman. Time became difficult for us, so Abdullah said to her: Sit down for Ka`a, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: He cannot be patient with her distress. And if anyone forces it, I will not be a witness or an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"4167","Al-Fadl bin Sahl told us, he said: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Kathir told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim On the authority of Kilab ibn Talid, that while he was sitting with Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, a messenger from Nafi` ibn Jubayr came to him, saying: Your cousin is reciting. Peace be upon you, and he says: How is the hadith you told me about Asma bint Umays? Saeed said: Tell him that Asma bint Umays told me that she heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “He cannot be patient with... No one will endure the hardships and hardships of the city, except that I will be a witness or an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"4168","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi reported, saying: Yahya told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq, he said: Zainab told me, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, “that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the trees between the two trees of Medina to be uprooted or knocked down.”"
"4169","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Indeed, Abraham sanctified the House of God and protected it, and I sanctified Medina between its two forests. Its game cannot be hunted nor its limbs cut off.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4170","Harun bin Saeed reported, saying: Khalid bin Nizar told us, saying: Al-Qasim bin Mabur told me, on the authority of Yunus, saying: Ibn Shihab said, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Omar, that Al-Sumaitah was a woman from Banu Laith bin Bakr, who was in the lap of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: I heard her telling Safiyya bint Abi Ubaid that she heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Who among you is able to die?” In the city and let him die there, for I will intercede for him or bear witness for him.”"
"4171","Qutayba bin Sa`id reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he used to say: If I saw Antelope in Medina grazing what it has planted. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What is between its two lions is forbidden.”"
"4172","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ammar, and Amr bin Ali reported, saying: Yahya told us, saying: Ammar al-Dahni told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The lists of my pulpit are rewards in Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4173","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Makki told us, saying: Abdullah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abdul Majeed bin Suhail bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “My pulpit This is on one of the pastures of Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4174","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What is between my house and my pulpit is one of the gardens of Paradise.”"
"4175","Qutayba bin Saeed and Al-Harith bin Miskin reported, as I read from him while I was listening, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ammar Al-Dahni, on the authority of Abu Salamah, On the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, what is between my house and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise,” in the hadith of Al-Harith “Between my grave” And my pulpit (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4176","Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali reported, saying: Muhammad bin Kathir told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Abu Saleh, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They beat the livers of camels and seek knowledge, but they do not find it.” A scholar more knowledgeable than the scholar of Medina.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is wrong but the correct thing is, Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abu Salih (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4177","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad informed us, he is Ibn Salam al-Tarsusi, he said: Ishaq told us, he is the trustworthy son of Yusuf al-Wasiti al-Azraq, he said: Sufyan told us, On the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was expelled from Mecca, he said Abu Bakr: They expelled their Prophet. Indeed, to Allah we belong, and to Him we shall return, that He may destroy us. Then permission was revealed to those who fight, saying that they have been wronged, and indeed God is powerful in their victory, so I knew that there would be a fight. Ibn Abbas said: It is the first verse that was revealed regarding the fight. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4178","Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq reported, he said: My father informed us, he said: Al-Hussein bin Waqid reported, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “Abd al-Rahman bin Awf and his companions came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Mecca, and they said: O Messenger of God, we are in might.” And we were polytheists, but when we believed we became humiliated. He said: I have been commanded to pardon, so do not fight. When God transferred him to Medina, he commanded you to fight, so desist. Then God revealed: Have you not seen those to whom it was said: “Restrain your hands and establish prayer” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4179","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, he said: Mu`tamar told us, he said: I heard Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, he said: I said on the authority of Sa`id? He said: Yes, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh and Al-Harith ibn Miskin reported, it was read to him, and the pronunciation is by Ahmad. He said: Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was sent With all the words, and I was helped by terror, and while I was sleeping the keys to the treasures of the earth were brought and placed in my hand.” Abu Hurairah said: So he went. By the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while you are taking it up, Harun bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Khaled, who is Ibn Nizar, he said: He informed me Al-Qasim bin Mabrur, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Towards him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4180","Kathir ibn Ubaid al-Homsi reported, saying: Muhammad ibn Harb told us, on the authority of al-Zubaidi, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, and Abu Salamah ibn Abdul Rahman, that Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “I was sent with the comprehensive words, and I was supported With terror, and while I was sleeping, the keys to the treasures of the earth were brought and placed in my hand.” Abu Hurairah said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went away. And peace be upon you while you pull it out (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4181","Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala and al-Harith ibn Miskin reported on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Saeed bin Al-Musayyab told me that Abu Hurairah told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was ordered to fight people until they say: There is no god but God, so whoever says: There is no god but God, his property and his soul will be protected from me, except according to his right and his account is with God.”"
"4182","Kathir bin Ubaid reported, on the authority of Muhammad bin Harb, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died and Abu Bakr was appointed as his successor, and whoever of the Arabs became infidels, Omar said: O Abu Bakr, how do you fight? The people? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I have been commanded to fight the people until they say there is no god but God, so whoever says: There is no god but God is protected from me. His wealth and his soul except according to his right, and his reckoning is with God. Abu Bakr said: By God, I will fight whoever differentiates between prayer and zakat, for zakat is a right. Money, by God, if they had withheld from me a she-hut that they were giving to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I would have fought them for withholding it, for by God it is not “Unless I saw that God had opened Abu Bakr’s chest to fight, I knew that it was the truth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4183","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah narrated to us Homsi, he said: Othman narrated to us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Ubaid Allah narrated to us, and Kathir bin Ubaid narrated to us. He said: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah bin Masoud, that Abu Hurairah, he said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died and Abu Bakr was after him, and the Arabs who disbelieved disbelieved, Omar said: Oh Abu Bakr, how do you fight people when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I have been commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but God, so whoever says: There is no god but God. His wealth and his soul have been protected from me except according to his right and his reckoning is with God. Abu Bakr said: I will fight whoever distinguishes between prayer and zakat. Zakat is the right of money, and by God, if they withhold from me a single hug that they used to give to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I will fight them for withholding it. Omar said: By God, it was only if I saw that God had opened Abu Bakr’s heart to fight, so I knew that it was the truth. And the wording is by Ahmad. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4184","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Mu’mal bin Al-Fadl told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, he said: Shuaib bin Abi Hamza told me, Sufyan bin Uyaynah, and another mentioned, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: “Abu Bakr agreed To fight them, and Omar said: O Abu Bakr, how do you fight the people when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I was ordered to fight the people until they say: No? There is no god but Allah. If they say it, their lives and their properties are protected from me, except by what is due to it. Abu Bakr said: I will fight whoever separates the prayers. And zakat, by God, if they had withheld from me a she-hut which they used to give to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, I would have fought them for withholding it. Omar said: By God, it was only when I saw that God had opened Abu Bakr’s heart to fight them that I knew it was the truth.”"
"4185","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Amr bin Asim told us, saying: Imran Abu Al-Awwam Al-Qattan told us, saying: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas bin Malik said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, the Arabs turned away. Omar said: O Abu Bakr, how do you fight the Arabs? Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, only said: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they bear witness that there is no god but God, and that I am the Messenger.” God, and establish prayer, and pay zakat. “By God, if they had withheld from me a hug that they used to give to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I would have fought them for it,” he said. Omar: When I saw Abu Bakr’s opinion explained, I knew that it was the truth.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Imran al-Qattan is not strong in hadith, and this hadith is wrong, as was the one before it, and the correct hadith is the hadith of al-Zuhri. On the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4186","Ahmad bin Muhammad informed me, he said: Uthman told us, on the authority of Shuaib, and Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir informed me, he said: My father told us, he said: Shuaib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab told me that Abu Hurairah told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “I have been commanded to fight the people until they say there is no god but God. Whoever says it has protected himself and his wealth from me, except according to what is due and his reckoning is with God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4187","Harun bin Abdullah and Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, saying: Yazid told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah reported, on the authority of Humaid, On the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Strive the polytheists with your wealth, your hands, and your tongues.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4188","Abdah bin Abdul Rahim informed me, he said: Salama bin Sulaiman informed me, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak informed me, he said: Wahib informed me, he said: Omar informed me. Ibn Muhammad Ibn Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Whoever dies and does not fight He did not talk to himself about any invasion, and he died in a state of hypocrisy.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4189","Ahmad bin Yahya bin Al-Wazir bin Sulayman reported, on the authority of Ibn Ufayr, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn Musafer, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salama Ibn Abd al-Rahman, and Sa`id Ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “By the One who With his hand, had it not been that men of the believers who do not like themselves should lag behind me and I cannot find anything to carry them to, I would not have lagged behind a company that is in the morning. For the sake of God, and by the One in Whose hand is my soul, I wished to be killed in the cause of God, then brought back to life, then killed, then brought back to life, then killed.”"
"4190","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ reported, saying: Bishr told us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sahl bin Sa’d. He said: I saw Marwan bin Al-Hakam sitting, so I came and sat next to him. He told us that Zayd bin Thabit told him, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” And a peace was sent down to him. Not equal are those who sit among the believers, other than those in need of harm and those who strive in the cause of God. Then Ibn Umm Maktum came and was imitating it. Ali, and he said: O Messenger of God, if I were able to wage jihad, I would wage war. So God sent down his thigh upon my thigh, and it became heavy on me to the point that I thought that You will graze my thigh, then I will walk away from it without being harmed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4191","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told us, he said: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab. He said: Sahl bin Saad told me, he said: I saw Marwan sitting in the mosque, so I approached and sat next to him, and he informed us that Zaid Ibn Thabit told him, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, dictated to him that those who were sitting among the believers are not equal, other than those in need of harm and the mujahideen.” For the sake of God, he said: Then Ibn Umm Maktum came and he was dictating it to me, and he said: O Messenger of God, by God, if I were able to wage jihad, I would wage war. He was a blind man, so God sent down the revelation to His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, while his thigh was on my thigh, and it became heavy until it almost touched my thigh. Then he walked. From him, then God revealed: “other than those destined to harm.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4192","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: “When it was revealed, it is not equal Those who were sitting among the believers, Ibn Umm Maktum, who was blind, came and said: O Messenger of God, how come I am blind? He said: So he continued until it came down \"not deserving of harm\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4193","Nasr bin Ali reported, saying: Al-Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned A word meaning, he said: “Bring me the shoulder and the tablet.” So it was written: Those of the believers who are sitting are not equal, and Amr bin Umm Maktum is behind him. He said: Do I have any permission? So I descended without being deprived of harm. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4194","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sufyan and Shu’bah, who said: Habib bin Abi Thabit told us, on the authority of Abu Abbas He is Al-Sa’ib bin Farukh, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: “A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asking his permission to engage in jihad. He said: Are your parents alive? He said: Yes. He said: So he struggled with them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4195","Abdul Wahhab bin Al-Hakam Al-Warraq reported, saying: Hajjaj reported, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, saying: Muhammad bin Talha, who is Ibn Abdullah, informed me. Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of his father Talha, on the authority of Muawiyah Ibn Jahimah al-Salami, “Jahimah came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Oh Messenger of God, I wanted to invade and I came to consult you. He said: Do you have a mother? He said: Yes. He said: Stay with her, for Paradise is at your doorstep. \"her legs\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4196","Kathir ibn Ubaid reported, saying: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, “that A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, which of the people is better? He said: A believer who strives with his life and his wealth in the cause of war? God said: Then who, O Messenger of God? He said: Then there is a believer among a people who fears God and shuns people from his evil."
"4197","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Abu Al-Khattab, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in the year of Tabuk addressing the people while leaning his back against his mount, so he said: Shall I inform you about the best of people and the worst of people? Indeed, one of the best of people is a man who works in the cause of God on the back of his horse, or on the back of his camel, or on the foot of him. Until death comes to him, and among the worst of people is an immoral man who reads the Book of God and does not pay heed to any of it.”"
"4198","Ahmad bin Sulaiman reported, saying: Ja’far bin Aoun told us, saying: Mis’ar reported, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Issa bin Talha, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “No one is tested by the fear of God and is fed by fire until the milk returns to the udder, nor “Dust will gather in the path of God, and smoke will gather in Hell in the nostrils of a Muslim forever.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4199","Hanad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Issa bin Talha, on the authority of Abu Hurairah On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “A man who has wept out of fear of God will not enter the Fire until the milk returns to the udder, and no dust is gathered in the path of God.” “And the smoke of the fire of hell.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4200","Issa bin Hammad reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A Muslim who kills an infidel, then kills an infidel, then attacks, and they approach, and dust will not gather in the belly of a believer. The path of God, and the flame of Hell, and the two do not coexist in the heart of the servant of faith and envy.”"
"4201","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Jarir reported, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of Safwan bin Abi Yazid, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Al-Lajlaj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No dust will ever gather in the path of God, nor smoke in the belly of a servant, nor will stinginess ever gather.” And faith is in the heart of a servant forever.”"
"4202","Amr bin Ali reported, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym. On the authority of Khaled ibn al-Lajlaj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “No dust or smoke shall gather in the face of God.” Never a man, and miserliness and faith will never coexist in the heart of a servant.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4203","Muhammad bin Amir reported, saying: Mansour bin Salamah told us, saying: Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Had, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Safwan bin Abi Yazid, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Al-Lajlaj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The “Dust in the path of God and the smoke of Hell are in the belly of a servant, and miserliness and faith cannot coexist in the heart of a servant.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4204","Amr bin Ali reported, saying: Arara bin Al-Barand and Ibn Abi Adi told us, saying: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Abi Yazid, On the authority of Husayn ibn al-Lajlaj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “No dust will gather in the path of God, and the smoke of hell will not gather in My nostrils are ever Muslim.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4205","Shuaib bin Yusuf told me, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Safwan bin Yazid, on the authority of Husayn bin Al-Lajlaj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No dust in the path of God nor the smoke of Hell shall gather in my nostrils.” A Muslim, and miserliness and faith cannot coexist in the heart of a Muslim man.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4206","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam reported, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Ja’far, on the authority of Safwan bin Yazid, On the authority of Abu Al-Ala bin Al-Lajlaj, that he heard Abu Hurairah say: “God does not collect dust in the path of God and the smoke of hell in the belly of a person.” A Muslim, and God does not combine in the heart of a Muslim both faith in God and stinginess.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4207","Abu Ammar told Al-Hussein Bin Harith, he said: Al-Walid Bin Muslim reported, he said: Yazid Bin Abi Maryam told us, he said: Abaya Bin Rafi’ joined me. Ibn Khadij, he said: I was walking to Friday prayer, and he said: Give good news, for these steps of yours are for the sake of God. I heard Abu Abbas, saying: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever’s feet become dusty in the path of God is forbidden to the Fire.”"
"4208","Isma bin Al-Fadl told me, he said: Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Shurayh, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Shamir al-Ru’ayni, He says: I heard Abu Ali al-Tajibi, saying: He heard Abu Rayhana, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “An eye was forbidden.” Over the Fire, I stayed up in the path of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4209","Abdah bin Abdullah reported, he said: Al-Hussein reported, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The morning and the soul in the path of God are better than the world and what is in it.”"
"4210","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Sa`id bin Abi Ayyub told us, he said: Sharhabeel bin Sharik Al-Maafiri told me, On the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli, that he heard Abu Ayyub al-Ansari say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “In the morning for the sake of God or a spirit that is better than anything over which the sun rises and sets.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4211","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid reported, on the authority of his father, saying: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari. On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Three of them all have a duty upon God to help him: the one who strives in the cause of God, and the one who marries.” The one who wants chastity, and the humble one who wants performance.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4212","Issa bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Ibn Wahb reported, on the authority of Makhramah, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Suhail bin Abi Salih, he said: I heard my father, He said: I heard Abu Hurairah saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The delegation of God is three: the invader, the pilgrim, and the pilgrim.”"
"4213","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin narrated a reading from him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik told me, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad. On the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God will provide for whoever strives in His way, He will not expel him from his house, except for jihad in his path and believing in his word that he will admit him to Paradise, or return him to his abode from which he left, along with what he obtained. reward or spoils\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4214","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Ata bin Mina, the client of Ibn Abi Dhubab, who heard Abu Hurairah say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God has appointed a mandate for whoever goes out in His path. Only faith in me and jihad in my path can get him out.” He is guaranteed until I admit him to Paradise, whichever it is, either through killing or death, or I return him to the abode from which he emerged. He has attained what he has attained. He attained any reward or spoils.”"
"4215","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir bin Dinar reported, saying: My father told us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Ibn Al-Musayyab told me, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “The example of a person who strives in the cause of God, and God knows best who is struggling.” In His path is like the example of a fasting person standing up, and God entrusts the one who strives in His path to cause him to die and admit him to Paradise, or to return him safely, including He attained any reward or spoils.”"
"4216","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid reported, saying: My father told us, he said: Haywa told us, and he mentioned another, saying: Abu Hani al-Khawlani told us, that He heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli saying: I heard Abdullah bin Amr saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “What Of a warrior who fights in the cause of God and captures spoils, unless they hasten two-thirds of their reward from the Hereafter, and a third remains for them. If they do not capture spoils. Their reward has been completed for them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4217","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Al-Hajjaj told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in what he narrated on the authority of his Lord, said: “Any of My servants who goes out and strives in My Way, seeking My pleasure, I guarantee for him If I take him back, I will return him with whatever reward or spoils he gained, and if I take him, I will forgive him and have mercy on him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4218","Hanad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The example of one who strives in the cause of God, and God knows best who strives in His cause is like the example of a fasting person who stands up.” “The humble one, the one who kneels and prostrates.”"
"4219","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jahadah told us, he said: Abu Husayn told me, that It was narrated to him that Abu Hurairah narrated to him, saying: “A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Show me a job that is just.” Jihad. He said: I do not find it. Are you able, when the mujahid comes out, to enter a mosque and stand up without let up and fast without breaking your fast? He said: Who can? That? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4220","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam reported, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Jaafar, he said: Urwa told me, On the authority of Abu Mawawih, on the authority of Abu Dhar, “He asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Which deed is best? He said: Faith in God and jihad in the path of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4221","Ishaq bin Mansour reported, he said: Abdul Razzaq reported, he said: Muammar reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “He asked A man asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Which deeds are best?” He said: “Belief in God.” He said: “Then what?” He said: “Then jihad for the sake of God.” He said: Then what? He said: Hajj Mabroor."
"4222","Al-Harith bin Miskin said: It was read to him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb. He said: Abu Hani told me, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman. Al-Hubli, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Abu Saeed, he who is satisfied with God as his Lord and with Islam religion, and through Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, as a prophet. Paradise was guaranteed for him. He said: Abu Sa’id marveled at it. He said: Give it back to me, O Messenger of God. So he did, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And there is another one by which the servant will be raised one hundred levels in Paradise, between every two levels, as shown. Heaven and earth. He said: What is it, O Messenger of God? He said: Jihad in the path of God, jihad in the path of God, jihad in the path of God. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4223","Harun bin Muhammad bin Bakkar bin Bilal told me, he said: Muhammad bin Isa bin Al-Qasim bin Sami informed me, he said: Zayd bin Waqid told us. He said: Busr bin Ubayd Allah told me, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever establishes prayer and pays zakat and dies not associating anything with God, it is incumbent upon God to forgive him if he emigrated or died during his birth. So we said: Oh. Messenger of God, will you not inform the people about it so that they may be given good tidings of it? He said: Indeed, Paradise is a hundred levels, and between every two levels He has prepared it. For those who strive in His cause, and were it not that I would make it difficult for the believers and find nothing to burden them with, and that their souls would not like to fall behind after me. I have never stayed behind a company, and I wished to be killed, then brought back to life, then killed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4224","Al-Harith bin Miskin said: I read it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Abu Hani told me, on the authority of Amr bin Malik Al-Janabi, that he heard Fadalah bin Ubaid, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “I am a leader and the leader is the bearer, to whom He believed in me and converted to Islam and migrated to a house in the outskirts of Paradise, and to a house in the middle of Paradise, and I am a leader for those who believe in me and submit to Islam and strive in the path of God. A house in the outskirts of Paradise, and a house in the middle of Paradise, and I am a leader for those who believe in me, submit to Islam, and strive in the cause of God, with a house in the outskirts of Paradise. And a house in the middle of Paradise and a house in the highest rooms of Paradise. Whoever does that will leave no search for good for good, nor any escape from evil. He will die where \"He wanted to die\""
"4225","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Abu Al-Nadr Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, he said: Abu Aqeel Abdullah bin Aqeel told us, he said: Musa told us Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Salim Ibn Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Sabra Ibn Abi Fakih, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The Satan sat down for the son of Adam in his ways, so he sat down for him in the path of Islam, and said: Become a Muslim and abandon your religion and the religion of your fathers and the fathers of your fathers. So he disobeyed him and converted to Islam. Then he sat for him on the way to migrate, and said: You will migrate and leave your land and your sky, but the likeness of an immigrant is like a horse in the middle, so he disobeyed him and migrated. Then he stopped for him on the path of jihad, and said: Jihad means the effort of oneself and one’s property, so you fight and are killed, then the woman is married and the money is divided. So he disobeyed him, so he struggled, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever does that has a right on God to admit him to Paradise, and whoever is killed has a right. It is upon God to admit him to Paradise. He said: And if he sweats, it is a duty on God to admit him to Paradise, or if an animal bites him, it is a duty on God to admit him to Paradise. He will admit him to Paradise.”"
"4226","Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad reported, saying: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Humaid bin Abd al-Rahman told him that Abu Hurairah used to narrate that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever spends two pairs for By God, we will be called in Paradise, O servant of God. This is good. Whoever is among the people of prayer will be called for the sake of prayer, and whoever is among the people of jihad will be called from. Chapter of jihad, and whoever was among the people of charity will be called from the gate of charity, and whoever was among the people of fasting will be called from the gate of Rayyan, so Abu Bakr said O Prophet of God, there is no necessity for the one who is called from those gates. Will anyone be called from all of those gates? He said: Yes, and I hope so \"You will be one of them\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4227","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, that Amr bin Murrah told them, he said: I heard Abu Wael, he said: Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari told us, he said: “A Bedouin came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: A man fights to be remembered, and he fights For the spoils, and he fights to see his place. Who is in the cause of God? He said: Whoever fights so that the word of God may be supreme is in the cause of God."
"4228","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Khaled told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Yunus bin Yusuf told me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, he said: The people dispersed to meet Abu Hurairah, and someone from the Levant said to him: O Sheikh, tell me a hadith that you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The first people to be judged on the Day of Resurrection are three: A man who was martyred and then brought. So he made known to him His blessings, and he recognized them. He said: What did you do there? He said: I fought for you until I was martyred. He said: You lied, but you fought because it would be said: So-and-so. Bold, as it was said, then he was ordered to be dragged on his face until he was thrown into the Fire, and a man who learned knowledge and taught it and read the Qur’an, so he was brought. So he made known to him his blessings, and he recognized them. He said: What did you do in it? He said: I learned knowledge and taught it and I recited the Qur’an in you. He said: You lied, but you learned knowledge. To be said: A scholar and you have read the Qur’an. To be said: A reader. So it was said. Then he was ordered to be dragged on his face until he was thrown into the Fire, and he is a man whom God has enlarged. And he gave him all kinds of wealth, so he was brought to him and showed him his blessings, so he recognized them, and said: What did you do with them? He said: I did not leave any way, meaning. You would not like for it to be spent on, unless I spent on it for you. He said: You lied, but you did so, so that it would be said: He is generous. It was said, then he was ordered to be drawn to his face until he was thrown into the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4229","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Jabla bin Atiya, on the authority of Ibn al-Walid bin Ubadah. Ibn al-Samit, on the authority of his grandfather, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever fights in the cause of God and does not intend to do anything except to bring back punishment, will get what he intended.”"
"4230","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah reported, on the authority of Jablah bin Atiyya, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Al-Walid, on the authority of Ubadah Ibn Al-Samit, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever fights and does not intend in his raids anything except a camel, has something \"He intended\""
"4231","Issa bin Hilal reported, saying: Muhammad bin Himyar told us, saying: Muawiyah bin Salam told us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Shaddad Abi Ammar, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili said: “A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Have you seen a man who went on a campaign, seeking reward and remembrance, what is his? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He has nothing. So he repeated it three times. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: He has nothing. Then he said: God does not accept any work except that which is sincerely for Him and seeking His Face thereby. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4232","Yusuf bin Saeed reported, saying: I heard Hajjaj, he said: Ibn Jurayj reported, saying: Suleiman bin Musa told us, he said: Malik bin Yakhamir told us, that Muadh bin Jabal told them that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever fights in the cause of God, from a Muslim man, and mounts a she-camel, must For him is Paradise, and whoever asks God for killing truthfully on his own behalf and then dies or is killed will have the reward of a martyr, and whoever is wounded in the way of God Or a calamity befalls, it will come on the Day of Resurrection as heavy as ever, its color like saffron and its scent like musk, and whoever sustains a wound in In the way of God, he has the mark of martyrs.”"
"4233","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir reported, saying: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Safwan, saying: Sulaym bin Amir told me, on the authority of Sharhabeel bin Al-Samat, that he said to Amr bin Absa: O Amr, tell us a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I heard the Messenger of God God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “Whoever turns gray hair in the cause of God, it will be for him light on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever shoots an arrow in the cause of God Whether he reaches the enemy or not, he will have the right to free a slave, and whoever frees a believing slave, his redemption from the Fire, limb by limb.”"
"4234","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala reported on the authority of Khalid, who said: Hisham told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Salim ibn Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ma’dan ibn Abu Talha, on the authority of Abu Najih al-Sulami, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever reaches an arrow will have a degree in Paradise, and sixteen arrows reached that day. He said: And I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whoever shoots an arrow in the way of God, it is \"liberated justice\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4235","Muhammad bin Al-Ala reported, saying: Abu Muawiyah told us, saying: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Sharhabeel Ibn Al-Samat, he said: He said to Ka’b Ibn Murrah: O Ka’b, tell us on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and beware. He said: I heard him say: “Who He turned gray hair in the cause of God, and it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection. He said to him: Tell us about the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and beware. He said: I heard him say : Shoot someone who reaches the enemy with an arrow, by which God will raise him in rank. Ibn al-Nahham said: O Messenger of God, and what is the rank? He said: But it is not At a threshold, but there are a hundred years between the two levels.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4236","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Al-Mu’tamir told us, saying: I heard Khalid, meaning Ibn Zayd, Aba Abdul-Rahman al-Shami, speaking about Shurahbil bin Al-Samat, on the authority of Amr bin Abasa, said: I said to him: O Amr bin Abasa, narrate to us a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. There is no forgetfulness or deficiency in him, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever shoots an arrow in the way of God If the enemy arrives, whether he makes a mistake or is injured, it is like the freedom of a slave, and whoever frees a Muslim slave, the redemption of every limb of him will be the same as a limb of the Fire. Hell, and whoever turns gray hair in the cause of God, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4237","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Al-Walid, on the authority of Ibn Jabir, on the authority of Abu Salam Al-Aswad, on the authority of Khalid bin Yazid, on the authority of Uqba bin Amer, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God admits three people to Paradise with one arrow. Its maker expects goodness in his making.” And the one who shoots it and the one who shoots it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4238","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “No.” He speaks to someone in the path of God, and God knows best who is spoken in His path, unless he comes on the Day of Resurrection and his wound is bloody, the color of which is the color of blood. And the smell is the smell of musk.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4239","Hanad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tha’labah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Coat them with their blood, for not a word is spoken about God except that on the Day of Resurrection his wound will bleed, the color of blood.” And its scent is the scent of musk.”"
"4240","Amr bin Sawad bin Al-Aswad bin Amr reported, saying: Ibn Wahb reported, saying: Yahya bin Ayyub informed me, and another person before him mentioned, On the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: “When it was the day of Uhud and the people took their place, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, greeted him in a certain area with twelve men from the Ansar, including Talha bin Ubaid Allah. The polytheists overtook him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned to May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Who are the people? Talha said: I. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: As are you? A man from the people said: Al-Ansar: It is me, O Messenger of God. He said: You. He fought until he was killed, then he turned and saw the polytheists. He said: Who are the people? Talha said: I, he said: As you are, then a man from the Ansar said: I, and he said: You, so he fought until he was killed, then he continued saying that and going out to them. A man from the Ansar, and he fought the same way as those before him, until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Talhah bin Ubaid Allah remained, so the Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Who is for the people? So Talha said: I am. So Talha fought like the eleven, until his hand was struck and his fingers were cut off. Talha said: He felt, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: If you had said: In the name of God, the angels would have exalted you and the people were watching, then the polytheists would be rejected."
"4241","Amr ibn Sawad ibn al-Aswad ibn Amr informed, he said: Ibn Wahb informed, he said: Yunus informed, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abd al-Rahman informed me. And Abdullah, Ibn Ka’b bin Malik, reported that Salama bin Al-Akwa’ said: “On the Day of Khaybar, my brother fought a fierce battle with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then his sword rebounded on him and killed him. The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said about that and doubted it: A man died by his own weapon. Salamah said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, arrived from Khaybar, and I said: O Messenger of God, do you permit me to come to you? So the Messenger of God gave me permission May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then Omar ibn al-Khattab said: I know what you are saying. He said: So I said: By God, had it not been for God, we would not have been guided, nor given charity, nor We prayed, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You have spoken the truth. So send down peace upon us and make our feet firm if we meet us while the polytheists have transgressed. Upon us. When I had finished my anger, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who said this? I said: My brother, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God have mercy on him, so I said: O Messenger of God, by God, some people fear praying for him. They say: A man died by his own weapon. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: He died striving, striving hard.” Ibn Shihab said: Then I asked Ibn Salamah ibn Al-Akwa’, and he told me on the authority of his father, like that, However, when I said: Some people fear praying for him, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: They lied. He died striving, striving, so for him His reward is double.” He pointed with his two fingers."
"4242","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed reported, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Yahya, he said: Dhakwan Abu Salih told us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Were it not that I would cause hardship to my nation, I would not leave behind a expedition, but they cannot find a load, and I cannot find anything to carry them, and it is difficult for me.” lest they lag behind me, and I wish I had been killed in the path of God, then brought back to life, then killed, then brought back to life three times.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4243","Amr bin Othman bin Saeed informed me, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Saeed bin Al-Musayyab informed me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, had it not been that there are men among the believers whose souls do not like to They lag behind me, and I cannot find anything to carry them with. As long as I leave behind a expedition that sets out in the path of God, by the One in Whose hand is my soul, I wish I were I am killed in the cause of God, then I am brought back to life, then I am killed, then I am brought back to life, then I am killed.”"
"4244","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed reported, saying: Baqiya told us, on the authority of Buhair, on the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Ibn Abi Amira, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is not among people a peaceful soul that its Lord has taken that would love to return to you. And for hers is the world and nothing in it except the martyr. Ibn Abi Amira said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Because I love to be killed in the name of God. To me that I may have people of goodness and piety.”"
"4245","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, Sufyan said: On the authority of Amr, he said: I heard Jabir, saying: “A man said on the day of Uhud: What do you think if I were killed in the cause of God? So where am I? He said: In Paradise. He said: Then he brought forth fruits that were in his hand, then he fought until he was killed. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4246","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Abu Asim told us, saying: Ibn Ajlan told us, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “A man came To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, as he was giving a sermon on the pulpit. He said: Have you considered that if I were killed in the path of God, patient and seeking reward, coming forward and not retreating, he would disbelieve? May God protect me from my bad deeds. He said: Yes, then he was silent for an hour, then he said: Where is the questioner above? The man said: Here I am, O Messenger of God. He said: What did you say? He said: Have you considered that if I were killed in the cause of God, patient and seeking reward, coming forward and not retreating, God would pardon my sins? \"Gabriel above\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4247","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin narrated a reading from him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik narrated to me, on the authority of Yahya Bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, he said: “A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted me, and said: O Messenger of God, if I were killed in the cause of God, patient, seeking reward, and not retreating, will God atone for me my sins, said the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Yes, and when the man turned away, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called him, or he gave orders for him to be called, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called for May God bless him and grant him peace: How did you say? So he repeated his statement, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Yes, except debt. That’s what he said to me. Gabriel (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4248","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of Abi Qatada that He heard him speaking on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “He stood up among them and mentioned to them that jihad in the path of God and belief in God is better.” Deeds, then a man stood up and said: O Messenger of God, do you think that if I were killed in the cause of God, my sins would be forgiven for me? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: Yes, if you are killed in the cause of God, and you are patient and seeking reward, advancing and not retreating. Then he said: How? I said: Have you seen if I were killed in the cause of God? Will my sins be expiated for me? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Yes, if you are killed in the cause of God and you are patient, seeking reward and coming forward, not retreating. Except for debt, for Gabriel said that to me.”"
"4249","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, he heard Muhammad bin Qais, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, He said: “A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was on the pulpit, and he said: O Messenger of God, what if I strike with this sword of mine for the sake of God is patient and seeking reward, advancing and not retreating until I am killed and my sins are expiated from me. He said: Yes. Then when he returned, he called him and said: This is Gabriel saying: Except? That you are in debt (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4250","Harun bin Muhammad bin Bakkar bin Bilal reported, saying: Muhammad bin Issa reported, saying: Zayd bin Waqid told us, on the authority of Kathir bin Murrah, that the worship of Ibn al-Samit told them that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is not a soul on earth that dies and has good with God that would like to return.” To you is the world, except for the murdered man, for he would love to come back and be killed again.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4251","Abu Bakr bin Nafi’ informed us, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Hammad, he is Ibn Salamah, told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “A man from the people of Paradise will be brought, and God will say: O son of Adam, how did you find your abode? Then He will say: O Lord, the best abode. He says: Ask and hope. Then he says: I ask you to bring me back to this world so that I may be killed in your cause ten times because of what he sees as the virtue of martyrdom."
"4252","Imran bin Yazid reported, saying: Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The martyr does not feel the touch of killing except as one of you feels the touch of a pinch and pinches it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4253","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Shurayh told me, that Sahl bin Abi Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif narrated to him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever asks God for testimony truthfully May God grant him the status of martyrs, even if he dies in his bed.”"
"4254","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Abdul-Rahman bin Shurayh told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tha’labah. Al-Hadrami, that he heard Ibn Hujayrah reporting, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “One-fifth of those who were arrested in Any of them is a martyr: He who is killed in the cause of God is a martyr, and he who drowns in the cause of God is a martyr, and he who is drowned in the cause of God is a martyr. “The one who is stabbed in the cause of God is a witness, and the one who gives childbirth in the cause of God is a witness.”"
"4255","Amr bin Uthman told me, he said: Baqiya told us, on the authority of Buhair, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Bilal, on the authority of Al-Irbad bin Sariyah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The martyrs and those who died on their beds dispute before our Lord regarding those who die from the plague, and He says Martyrs: Our brothers were killed as we were killed, and those who died in their beds say: Our brothers died in their beds as we died, so our Lord says: Look at their wounds, for if their wounds resemble the wounds of those who were killed, then they are from them and with them, so their wounds resemble their wounds.”"
"4256","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “ God marvels at two men, one of whom kills his friend, and He said again: Let him laugh at two men, one of whom kills his friend, and then they enter. Paradise (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4257","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin reported a reading about him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik told me, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, On the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God laughs at two men, one of whom kills the other. Both of them He will enter Paradise. This man will fight in the way of God and be killed. Then God will turn to the killer and he will fight and be martyred.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4258","Issa bin Hammad told us, he said: Al-Layth informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They will not come together in Hell. A Muslim kills an infidel, then he kills an infidel and approaches. They will not come together in the belly of a believer. Dust in the path of God and the blaze of Hell, and the two do not coexist in a servant: faith and envy.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4259","Al-Harith bin Miskin said it was read on the authority of Ibn Wahb. He said: Abd al-Rahman bin Shurayh informed me, on the authority of Abd al-Karim bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Ubaydah bin Uqba, on the authority of Sharhabeel bin Al-Samat, on the authority of Salman Al-Khair, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “ Whoever works in the cause of God for a day or night will have the reward of fasting and praying for a month, and whoever dies while stationed will have a similar reward. And sustenance was granted to him and he was safe from temptation.”"
"4260","Amr bin Mansour reported, saying: Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, saying: Al-Layth told us, saying: Ayyub bin Musa told me, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Shurahbil bin Al-Samat, on the authority of Salman, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever continues in the path of God day or night For him, it is like fasting for a month and praying in prayer, so if he dies, the work he was doing will be done for him, and the temptation will be safe, and his livelihood will be rewarded for him.”"
"4261","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Zahra bin Ma’abad, he said: Abu Salih told me A servant of Othman, he said: I heard Othman bin Affan, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “A day’s bond in the path of God.” “It is better than a thousand days in any other dwelling.”"
"4262","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Ma’n told us, he said: Zahra bin Ma`bad, on the authority of Abu Salih, the servant of Uthman, who said: Uthman said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “A day in the path of God is good.” than a thousand days other than that.”"
"4263","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin reported a reading of it, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, who said: Malik told me, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: “Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to Quba, he would visit Umm Haram bint Milhan. So she fed him, and Umm Haram bint Milhan was under Ubadah ibn al-Samit, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon her one day. So she fed him and sat down to scrub his head, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell asleep and then woke up laughing. She said: So I said: What makes you laugh? O Messenger of God? He said: People from my nation were presented to me as raiders in the cause of God riding on this sea as kings on the throne, or something like that. Kings over families. Ishaq doubted, so I said: O Messenger of God, pray to God to make me one of them. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed for her. He said hello, then he woke up and laughed, so I said: O Messenger of God, what makes you laugh? He said: Some of my nation were presented to me as warriors in God’s cause as kings over me. Dynasties, or like kings over dynasties, as he said at the beginning. So I said: O Messenger of God, pray to God to make me one of them. He said: You are one of them. The first two, she rode the sea in the time of Muawiyah, and she was thrown off her mount when she came out of the sea, and she perished.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4264","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi reported, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, on the authority of Umm Haram bint Milhan, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to us and said: We are with us, then he woke up laughing, so I said: O Messenger of God, my mother and father, what made you laugh? He said: I saw people from my nation riding this sea like kings on beds. I said: Pray. May God make me one of them. He said: Then you are one of them. Then he fell asleep and then woke up laughing. I asked him, and he said the same as what he said. I said: So pray to God to make me one of them. He said: You are among the first. So Ubadah ibn al-Samit married her, so he rode into the sea, and she rode with him. When she came, a mule was presented to her, and she rode it and knocked it down, causing its neck to be broken.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4265","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim reported, saying: Zakaria bin Adiy told us, saying: Ubayd Allah bin Amr reported, on the authority of Zaid bin Abi Unaisah, on the authority of Sayyar, Zakaria said: And Hushaym foretold it, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Jabr ibn Ubaidah, and Ubayd Allah said: On the authority of Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, promised us the Battle of India. If he achieves it, I will spend my life and my money there, but if I am killed, I will be one of the “The best of martyrs, and if I return, I will be the liberated Abu Hurairah.”"
"4266","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Sayyar Abu al-Hakam told us, on the authority of Jabr bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, promised us the expedition to India, so if I reach it, I will spend my life therein.” And what about me? If I am killed, I will be the best of martyrs, and if I return, then I will be Abu Hurairah the Liberated.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4267","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim told us, he said: Asad bin Musa told us, he said: Baqiya bin al-Walid told us, he said: Abu Bakr told me Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of his brother Muhammad bin Al-Walid, on the authority of Luqman bin Amir, on the authority of Abd al-A’la bin Adiy al-Bahrani, on the authority of Thuban’s servant The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Two bands from my nation, a band that is invading India, and a band “You will be with Jesus, son of Mary.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4268","Issa bin Yunus al-Ramli al-Fakhouri reported, saying: Damra told us, on the authority of Abu Zar’ah al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Sakina, a man from among the muharrins, on the authority of a man From the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the digging of the trench, a rock appeared to them blocking Between them and the pits, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up, took the pick, placed his robe towards the trench and struck, and said: And the word of your Lord has been fulfilled in truth and justice. There is no one who can alter His words, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing. So a third of the stone rolled down, and Salman the Persian was standing watching, and it flashed with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, struck with a stroke of lightning, then he struck the second time and said: And the word of your Lord has been fulfilled in truth and justice. There is no one who can change His words. And He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing. So the other third struck and a flash of lightning flashed that Salman could see. Then he struck the third, and said: And the word of your Lord has been completed in truth and justice. He changes His words, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing. Then the remaining third came and flashed brightly, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out and took his robe. And he sat down. Salman said: O Messenger of God, I saw that when you struck, you would not strike unless there was a spark with it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him. Peace be upon him: O Salman, did you see that? He said: Yes, by the One who sent you with the truth, O Messenger of God. He said: When I struck the first, my debts were raised for me? Khosrau and its environs and many cities until I saw them with my own eyes. Then one of his companions who were present said to him: O Messenger of God, pray to God to He will conquer it against us, make their descendants spoil us, and destroy their country with our hands. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for that, and then I struck the second plague, and Caesar's Cities and their surroundings were raised to me until I saw them with my own eyes. He said: O Messenger of God, pray to God to open them. upon us, and their descendants will give us spoils. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called, then I struck the third time, and the cities of Abyssinia and what There were villages around it until I saw it with my own eyes, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said at that: Leave the Abyssinians as long as they leave you, and leave “The Turks have not left you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4269","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not “The hour is when the Muslims will fight the Turks, a people whose faces are like hammering shields, who wear hair and walk in hair.”"
"4270","Muhammad bin Idris reported, saying: Omar, who is Ibn Hafs bin Ghayath, narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Musab bin Sa’d. On the authority of his father, he thought that he had superiority over the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God only helps this weak nation, through their supplications, prayers, and sincerity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4271","Yahya bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir told us, he said: Omar bin Abdul Wahid told us, he said: Ibn Jabir told us, he said: Zaid bin Abdul Wahid told me. Artaat Al-Fazari, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr Al-Hadrami, that he heard Abu Darda’ say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “Seek Me for the weak, for it is only through your weak that you are provided for and helped.”"
"4272","Sulaiman bin Dawud and Al-Harith bin Miskin reported a reading from him, while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb. He said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me, On the authority of Bukair ibn al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Busr ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Zayd ibn Khalid, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever prepares an invader in For the sake of God, he has fought, and whoever succeeds him with good in his family has fought.”"
"4273","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi, who said: Harb bin Shaddad told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah. He is Ibn Abd Al-Rahman, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prepares a invader in For the sake of God, he has fought, and whoever leaves behind a fighter doing good to his family has fought.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4274","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Abdullah bin Idris reported, saying: I heard Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, narrating on the authority of Amr bin Jawan, On the authority of Al-Ahnaf ibn Qais, he said: “We went out as pilgrims and came to Medina, intending to perform Hajj. While we were in our homes, we placed our saddlebags when they came to us.” He was coming, and he said: The people had gathered in the mosque and were terrified. He said: So we set off, and behold, people were gathered together in a group in the middle of the mosque, and then Ali And Talha, and Al-Zubayr, and Saad bin Abi Waqqas, so we are like that when Othman came, wearing a yellow sheet with which he covered his head. He said: Is it Ali? Is it Talha? Is it Saad? Is it Saad? Is it I? Do you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever buys the land of the son of so-and-so, God will forgive him, so I buy it for twenty thousand.” Or twenty-five thousand. So I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I informed him, and he said: Place it in our mosque and its reward is yours. They said: Oh God, yes. He said: I adjure you by God, besides whom there is no god. Do you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever buys Bir Rumah, may God forgive him, so I bought it for such-and-such, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I bought it for such-and-such. And so on. He said: Make it a source of water for the Muslims and its reward is yours. They said: Oh God, yes. He said: I adjure you by God, besides whom there is no god. Do you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at the faces of the people and said: Whoever prepares these people, may God forgive him, meaning the army of hardship. So I prepared them so that they were not missing a head or a belt. They said: Oh God, yes. He said: Oh God, bear witness. Oh God, bear witness."
"4275","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin reported a reading about him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim. He said: Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab. On the authority of Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever spends two pairs in the cause of God will be called.” Paradise, O Abdullah, this is better. Whoever is among the people of prayer will be called for the sake of prayer, and whoever is among the people of jihad will be called for the sake of jihad. And whoever was among the people of charity will be called from the gate of charity, and whoever was among the people of fasting will be called from the gate of Rayyan. Abu Bakr said: Is there anyone who He is called from these gates out of necessity. Is anyone called from all of these gates? He said: Yes, and I hope that you will be one of them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4276","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir reported, saying: Baqiya told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Yahya told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, He said: Abu Salamah told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever spends two pairs of wives in the path of God, she will supplicate him.” The keeper of every gate of Paradise: O so-and-so, come and enter. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, that is the one I intend to do, so he said. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “I hope that you will be one of them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4277","Ismail bin Masoud told me, he said: Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Sa’sa’a bin Muawiyah, he said: I found Abu Dharr, he said: I said: Tell me, he said: Yes, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No Muslim servant spends of all his wealth.” A couple for the sake of God, except that the barrier of Paradise will overtake him. They will all invite him to what he has. I said: How is that? He said: If they were camels Then two camels, and if there are cows, then two cows.”"
"4278","Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Nadr reported, saying: Abu Al-Nadr told us, saying: Ubayd Allah Al-Ashja’i told us, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Al-Rukin Al-Fazari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Yasir ibn Umaila, on the authority of Khuraym ibn Fatik Al-Asadi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “ “Whoever spends an effort in the way of God, it will be rewarded seven hundred times.”"
"4279","Bishr ibn Khalid reported, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja’far reported, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Sulayman, he said: I heard Abu Amr al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Masoud. “A man gave in charity a mounded she-camel for the sake of God, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: On the Day of Resurrection you will bring seven One hundred mottled camels.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4280","Amr ibn Uthman reported, saying: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Buhair, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Bahriyya, on the authority of Muadh ibn Jabal, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Conquest is conquest: as for he who seeks the face of God, obeys the imam, spends generously, and is pleased with his partner, And he avoids corruption, for his sleep and his awakening are all rewarded. As for whoever invades out of hypocrisy and reputation, disobeys the Imam, and spreads corruption on earth, then he will not He returns with subsistence.”"
"4281","Al-Hussein bin Harith and Mahmoud bin Ghaylan reported, and the wording is from Hussein. He said: Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Suleiman. Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The sanctity of the women of the Mujahideen to those sitting is like the sanctity of their mothers. There is no man who leaves behind the wife of a mujahideen man and betrays him in her, but he will stand by him on the Day of Resurrection and take from her work whatever he wants. What do you think?"
"4282","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Harami bin Amara told me, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Suleiman bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The sanctity of the women of the Mujahideen over those sitting is like the sanctity of their mothers. He succeeded him among his family and betrayed him. It will be said to him on the Day of Resurrection: This man betrayed you among your family, so take from his good deeds whatever you want. What do you think?"
"4283","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman reported, saying: Sufyan told us, he said: Qa’nab Kufi told us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The women of the Mujahideen are inviolable to those sitting in the sanctity like their mothers, and there is no A man from among the people who remained behind leaves a man among the mujahideen behind in his family and betrays him, except that an ambush will be made against him on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said: O so-and-so, this is so-and-so, take it. Whatever you want of his good deeds, then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, turned to his companions and said: What do you think he will leave behind any of his good deeds? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4284","Ahmad bin Abdul-Wahid told us, he said: Marwan al-Tatri told us, he said: Khaled bin Yazid bin Saleh bin Subaih al-Marri informed us, he said: Ibrahim bin Abi Abla told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul Rahman Al-Jurashi, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Salama bin Nufail Al-Kindi, He said: “I was sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man said: O Messenger of God, the people humbled the horses and laid down their weapons and said: No.” Jihad The war had ended, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned to face him and said: They lied, now the fighting has come, and no There will cease to exist from my nation a nation that fights for the truth, and God will cause the hearts of some people to turn aside for them, and will provide for them from Him until the Hour comes, or until the Day comes. God's promise, and the horses are tied to their forelocks of goodness until the Day of Resurrection, and it suggests to me that I will be arrested and not delayed, and you are excommunicated “You strike the necks of others, and the home of the believers is the Levant.”"
"4285","Amr bin Yahya bin Al-Harith reported, saying: Mahboub bin Musa told us, saying: Abu Ishaq reported, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Horses have goodness tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection. It is a reward for a man, it is a cover for a man, and it is a burden for a man. As for what it is for him, it is the one who seeks it for the sake of God. And he takes it as his own and does not hide anything in its bellies, but it is written for him for everything that is hidden in its bellies, a reward, even if a pasture presents itself to it.” Hadith"
"4286","I am Muhammad bin Salamah, and Al-Harith bin Miskin. A reading of it while I was listening, and the pronunciation is his. On the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abu Salih al-Samman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Horses are for a man a reward, and for another man there is a reward.” A covering, and on one man is a burden. As for the one for whom it is a reward, a man bound her in the path of God and prolonged for her a meadow or a meadow, and she did not achieve it. In her length of time in the meadow or in the garden, there would have been good deeds for him, and if she had interrupted that length of time and was waiting for one or two honors, it would have been Its effects: And in the hadith of Al-Harith, its effects are good deeds for him, and if it had passed by a river and drank from it, he would not have wanted it to be watered, that would have been the case. Good deeds are a reward for him, and a man who does them with singing and self-control and does not forget God’s rights over their necks or their backs, for that is a cover. And a man associated it with pride, hypocrisy, and distress to the people of Islam, so it is a burden, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about donkeys and he said: Why? Nothing has been sent down to me in it except this comprehensive, unique verse: “So whoever does an atom’s weight of good will see it.” {7} And whoever does an atom’s weight of evil will see it. He sees {8} \" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4287","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told me, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Orouba On the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: “There was nothing more beloved to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, than women.”"
"4288","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar told us, he said: Yazid bin Abi Habib told me, on the authority of Suwayd bin Qais, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Hudayj, on the authority of Abu Dharr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no Arabian horse that does not give the call to prayer.” Two supplications to him at every dawn: Oh God, you have made me the one whom You have granted me among the children of Adam, and made me his, so make me the most beloved of his family and his wealth. To him or to whomever he loves, his family and wealth to him.”"
"4289","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ al-Naysaburi informed us, saying: Abu Ahmad al-Bazzaz Hisham ibn Sa`id informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Muhajir al-Ansari informed us, on the authority of Aqeel bin Shabib, on the authority of Abu Wahb, who was a companion of his, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Call them names. The prophets, and the most beloved names to God, Abdullah, and Abdul-Rahman, and mount the horses and wipe their forelocks and their hooves and imitate them, And do not imitate it with the strings, and you must use every quantity whether it is darker-colored, or blond, darker-colored, or darker-colored, darker-colored.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4290","Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja`far informed us, he said: Shu`bah told us, and Ismail bin Masoud informed us, he said: Bishr told us, he said: Shu'bah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Zar'ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, hated forms of Of horses,” the wording refers to Ishmael (Peace Be Upon Him)"
